## Exercise

Regular exercise is one of the best things you can do. It can improve movement, balance, mood and sleep. Walking, cycling, dance, tai chi and boxing classes for Parkinson's are all popular.

## Preventing falls

Turn slowly, keep your home clutter free, and ask about a **falls assessment**. See [home adaptations and equipment](/support/home-and-equipment/).

## Eating and swallowing

Eat plenty of fibre and drink fluids to help constipation. If you have trouble swallowing, ask for a speech and language therapy referral. Protein can affect how levodopa works for some people. Ask your team about timing meals.

## Mood and sleep

Depression, anxiety and sleep problems are part of Parkinson's, not a sign of weakness. Tell your team, as they can be treated.

## Driving

You must tell the **DVLA** if you have Parkinson's. Many people carry on driving for years.

## For carers

Family carers can ask for a carer's assessment. See [help for carers](/support/carers/).

## Support

**Parkinson's UK** runs a free helpline, local groups and exercise classes.
